// Power-supply synthesis S3: cost profile ranked by the REAL catalogue
// price of the regulator (via the jlcparts provider's mpn_query, variant-
// preferred to the 3.3V part). 5V → 3.3V @ 100mA: an LDO and both bucks
// pass every capability gate; LP2985 (~$0.10, 0 support parts,
// P_pass ≈ 0.17W ≤ 400mW/2) beats TPS54331 (~$0.34) and the LM2596 clone
// (~$0.27) — and would still win the part-count fallback if the catalogue
// DB were absent (that fallback is stated in the survey, never silent).
// `balanced` ranks by loss instead (see test_supply_auto).

board SupplyLdoS3 {
    power VIN_5V = 5V @ 1A;
    power VCC_3V3 = 3.3V @ 100mA;
    ground GND;

    supply @VCC_3V3 from @VIN_5V {
        ripple_max: 50mV;
        profile:    cost;
    }
}
